                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "df7831a6-f8ad-44b0-9fc6-f81a8f451ebd",
                        "entry_id": "bd6ee227-2acb-3363-b916-c22a1bb780f9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "enols"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa3fd3f5-d637-3370-8a2f-9f7361aa84d2",
                        "entry_id": "bd6ee227-2acb-3363-b916-c22a1bb780f9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An organic compound containing a hydroxyl group bonded to a carbon atom which is doubly bonded to another carbon atom."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6802c745-8b7a-473a-b0cb-b4e9855d3d82",
                                "sense_id": "fa3fd3f5-d637-3370-8a2f-9f7361aa84d2",
                                "text": "1996, Ludvik Labler, August Rüttimann, Alfred Giger, Chapter 2: Coupling Reactions: Part I: Enol Ether and Aldol Condensations, George Britton, Synnove Liaaen-Jensen, Hanspeter Pfander (editors), Carotenoids, Volume 2: Synthesis, Springer (Birkhäuser), page 27,\nSince research on the total synthesis of carotenoids began, the enol ether and the aldol condensations have been frequently used for the formation of carbon-carbon double bonds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dbab7e3a-7e8e-41ba-8a90-4c7b5309fb43",
                                "sense_id": "fa3fd3f5-d637-3370-8a2f-9f7361aa84d2",
                                "text": "A solution to the use of the thermodynamic ketone enolate lies in the selective formation and reaction of silyl enol ethers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af00087c-017e-4b81-9970-a05ee87918f4",
                                "sense_id": "fa3fd3f5-d637-3370-8a2f-9f7361aa84d2",
                                "text": "It is interesting to note that relative enol stability (pK_E) plays little or no role in the relative acidity of enols for example, as in the case of 45 and 45’²⁴³."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "789ab647-ab04-4d34-bd5d-f784dc6b394b",
                        "source_entry_id": "bd6ee227-2acb-3363-b916-c22a1bb780f9",
                        "source_sense_id": "fa3fd3f5-d637-3370-8a2f-9f7361aa84d2",
                        "source_sense_description": "compound containing a hydroxyl group bonded to a carbon atom which is doubly bonded to another carbon",
                        "target_lang_word": "énol",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "énol",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2db85009-13ad-3970-b8d3-8b6dd37ef9ed",
                                        "entry_id": "3882b8b6-e2cc-387a-ac0a-7a2bef727487",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alcène comportant une fonction alcool."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea951139-0ebf-4b01-88fe-4820ef69e005",
                                                "sense_id": "2db85009-13ad-3970-b8d3-8b6dd37ef9ed",
                                                "text": "En principe, la thymine peut se tautomériser et se présenter également sous la forme d’énol (un alcène avec une fonction alcool), en plus de la forme plus courante de lactame."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
